## 10. Required agent behavior

1. When adding a workforce capability, state which of §1 through §7 it serves and
 what evidence row it produces.
2. Never add a person-shaped table without the scope-basis fields in §3.
3. Treat §4 as an architectural invariant. Before changing anything about
 identity, ask whether an existing attestation could end up pointing at a
 different person or at nothing.
4. Land grading with its threshold and attempt history in the same change set.
 A score with no recorded threshold cannot be re-derived later.
5. Report schema separately from delivery, and keep §9 current in the same
 change set that moves a row.
6. Mirror this rule to `core-assets/.cursor/rules/` when editing the workspace
 copy — the workspace `.cursor` directory is not a git root
 ([`auto-commit-push.mdc`](auto-commit-push.mdc)).

## Worked violation to fix

**Violation.** A release adds workforce import from CSV, assigns a document to
everyone in the file, and emails a link. The binder gains a training section
where an operator types the completion percentage. Attestations store the
signer's email as the key. Later the customer connects an identity provider, the
workforce is re-imported from it, and every person gets a new row.

Four failures. Roster rows carry no scope basis, so the completeness question
has no answer. The binder number is a typed claim, not evidence. Email as the
attestation key breaks the moment somebody marries or changes employer. And the
re-import orphaned every prior attestation, destroying exactly the audit trail
the program existed to create.

**Fix.** Capture scope basis, decider, and timestamp at import, and record
considered exclusions. Derive the binder section from the assignment ledger at
render time with the denominator explained. Bind attestations to the person
record while denormalizing signer identity at signing. Make federation a linking
operation against existing person rows, keyed on issuer and subject, so history
stays intact and a person can hold a local and a federated binding at once.

